<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boso of Provence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 844–887</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Boso of Vienne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boso was a Frankish noble who in 879 became the first king outside the Carolingian family since 751. Brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, he was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> and duke in Provence, and after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-stammerer">Louis the Stammerer</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and nobles meeting at Mantaille elected him king of Provence, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burgundy">Lower Burgundy</a>. The Carolingian kings besieged Vienne in 880–82, but he kept part of his realm until his death in 887.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence.jpg" alt="Boso of Provence" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Boson_of_Provence.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
